  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CCT- Tuwajibike (Let&#x2019;s be Accountable)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tuwajibike (let&#x2019;s be Accountable) project overall goal is improved public services delivery due to increased citizen and civil society agency to demand government&#x2019;s transparency and accountability. The project aims to strengthen citizen-led accountability and inclusive governance across five regions: Dodoma, Kigoma, Shinyanga, Tabora, and Pwani by pursuing three interlinked objectives. First, it will revitalize and support functional PETS and SAM Committees to monitor and report on the use of public resources, ensuring that local communities have the tools and capacity to track government spending and advocate for improved services. Second, it will facilitate meaningful engagement between community representatives and Local Government Authorities through interfaith dialogues and public accountability forums, creating safe and inclusive spaces for joint problem-solving. Lastly, the project will build the capacity of rights-holders particularly women, youth, and persons with disabilities by equipping them with knowledge on governance processes and participation rights, enabling them to effectively engage in decision-making and advocate for their specific needs.</narrative>
  </description>
